  "title": "merge: Treat no tsresol option as 6 when comparing IDBs",
  "description": "An IDB that lacks the if_tsresol option is treated as having a\ntimestamp resolution of 6 (microseconds). So if one IDB has a\nnon-6 tsresol option value and the other has no tsresol option,\nthose should be treated as different for merging purposes.\nConversely, if one IDB has an explicit tsresol option of 6 and\nthe other has no tsresol option, but they are otherwise identical,\nthey are the same interface. (Some libraries, including wiretap,\nmight remove a redundant TSRESOL of 6.)",
